  "describe": "Title 'The double helix' and 'B-DNA · 10 base pairs a turn · 3.4 nm a turn'; a leaning double helix of grey-blue beads on a string, two turns, its rungs half coral and half amber (A-T) or half blue and half teal (G-C); below, the sequence '5′ ATGCGTACCGATTAGCCTAG 3′', a four-colour legend and an 'Unzip' button. Later it has turned; a drag turns it further. After tapping Unzip the strands part from the top down (mid-way: a fork, the top half open, each half-rung on its own strand), and the button reads 'Zip up'. Mono: white (or black) hidden-line wireframes.",
